From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: wait for the link to stop before gating the clock

On a runtime suspend with clock stop, the controller broadcasts
ClockStopNow and the driver gates its clock straight away, while the
link can still be running. Devices that lose the clock before the link
has stopped lose sync when it comes back: they drop to device number 0
and are enumerated again, with bus clashes and parity errors on the
way, and that enumeration now and then fails or hangs, leaving the
headphones silent until a later resume.

Keep the clock on until the controller reports the link stopped, as the
vendor driver does (100 us, then poll every 500 us, for up to about 50
ms), and warn if it does not stop. Skip the wait when no device
acknowledged the clock stop, and on controllers up to v1.5.1, which do
not report the link state.

On the Pocket FIT's WCD9395 RX bus, 40 suspend and resume cycles with a
stream open found the link still running at the clock cut in 22
suspends and dropped the devices on 19 resumes, all after one of those
22, with 6 bus clashes and 4 parity errors. With the wait, 40 cycles on
the same boot dropped them on none, with no clashes or parity errors.
---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -872,6 +872,33 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The link can keep running briefly after ClockStopNow; gating the clock
+ * then makes the devices lose sync on resume. v1.5.1 and older do not
+ * report the link state.
+ */
+static void swrm_wait_for_clock_stop(struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl)
+{
+	int retry = SWRM_LINK_STATUS_RETRY_CNT;
+	u32 comp_sts = 0;
+
+	if (ctrl->version <= SWRM_VERSION_1_5_1)
+		return;
+
+	usleep_range(100, 105);
+
+	do {
+		ctrl->reg_read(ctrl, ctrl->reg_layout[SWRM_REG_FRAME_GEN_ENABLED],
+			       &comp_sts);
+		if (!(comp_sts & SWRM_FRM_GEN_ENABLED))
+			return;
+
+		usleep_range(500, 510);
+	} while (retry--);
+
+	dev_warn_ratelimited(ctrl->dev, "link still up after the clock stop\n");
+}
+
 static bool swrm_wait_for_frame_gen_enabled(struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl)
 {
 	int retry = SWRM_LINK_STATUS_RETRY_CNT;
@@ -1848,6 +1875,9 @@
 			dev_err(dev, "bus clock stop failed %d", ret);
 			return ret;
 		}
+
+		if (ret != -ENODATA)
+			swrm_wait_for_clock_stop(ctrl);
 	}
 
 	clk_disable_unprepare(ctrl->hclk);
